# WS2-03. # Sources: spec/03-ownership.md §3 (moves; a moved value is never dropped), §5 (drop order: locals in reverse declaration order, struct fields in declaration order, array elements first to last, parameters after the body locals; drops on every return/break/continue; exactly once), spec/04-expressions.md §3 (temporaries drop at statement end in reverse creation order).
 A loop-carried value moved and re-initialized each iteration; the
# last value is dropped once at scope end.
profiles: host
with: tok.clo
expect: output
contrast: a = tok(i + 2); ==> a = tok(i + 5);
contrast-expect: output
--- output
use 1
drop 1
use 2
drop 2
use 3
drop 3
use 4
end
drop 4
--- contrast-output
use 1
drop 1
use 5
drop 5
use 6
drop 6
use 7
end
drop 7
